        "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\u03a6(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X\u223cN(2,25),$ compute $P(-0.65<X<-0.25).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.2981\\,$ | $\\,0.2946\\,$ | $\\,0.2912\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.3336\\,$ | $\\,0.3300\\,$ | $\\,0.3264\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.3707\\,$ | $\\,0.3669\\,$ | $\\,0.3632\\,$ |",
        "worked_solution": "Given a normal random variable $X\u223cN(\\mu ,{\\sigma }^{2}),$ we have\n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)=P(\\frac{a-\\mu }{\\sigma }<Z<\\frac{b-\\mu }{\\sigma })\n$$\n\nwhere $Z\u223cN(0,1)$ is a standard normal random variable. In our case, we have $\\mu =2$ and $\\sigma =\\sqrt{25}=5.$\n\nFirst, we transform $X$ into a standard normal random variable $Z$ by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.65<X<-0.25) & =P(\\frac{-0.65-2}{5}<Z<\\frac{-0.25-2}{5}) \\\\  & =P(-0.53<Z<-0.45)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070250/assets/3d73cc4661eb9f68f636803918b3e55942e6538e4e70d13277d125386dad257e.png)\n\nNow, we express the required probability in terms of $\u03a6(z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.53<Z<-0.45) & =P(Z<-0.45)-P(Z\\le -0.53) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le -0.45)-P(Z\\le -0.53) \\\\  & =\u03a6(-0.45)-\u03a6(-0.53)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u03a6(-0.53) & =0.2981 \\\\ \u03a6(-0.45) & =0.3264\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.53<Z<-0.45) & =\u03a6(-0.45)-\u03a6(-0.53) \\\\  & =0.3264-0.2981 \\\\  & =0.0283.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(-0.65<X<-0.25)=0.0283.\n$$",
